The quotient ring $\mathbb{Z}_3[x]/(x^3 + x^2 + c)$ is a field if and only if the polynomial $x^3 + x^2 + c$ is irreducible over $\mathbb{Z}_3$. Since the polynomial has degree 3, it is irreducible if and only if it has no roots in $\mathbb{Z}_3 = \{0, 1, 2\}$. Evaluating the polynomial for each possible value of $c \in \{0, 1, 2\}$ reveals that $c=0$ has roots $0, 2$, $c=1$ has a root $1$, and only $c=2$ has no roots ($p(0)=2, p(1)=1, p(2)=2$). Thus, $c=2$ is the only solution in $\mathbb{Z}_3$, which corresponds to option B.

